# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# D-103: a callable-merge host that can throw -- its declaration `size_t: big (n)` needs a
# conversion whose receiver can throw -- has the declared-throw ABI: its return is the status and
# the node goes out through l2_out_result.  Before, the node was returned as the status (gcc: "returning
# 'void *' from a function with return type 'int'") and met the caller as a throw number: "lmx: walk
# error: unknown status", exit 3.  add5(1) = 6.  Mutant: the node returned as the status again.
# Entry 7.  (Under the knob the same text is unit_walk_make_adder_native_note.)
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    size_t: big (n)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN

@: add5 makeAdder(5)
int: a (add5: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 6
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
